  {
    "title": "EDUCATION AND GEOGRAPH",
    "department": "EDUCATION",
    "status": "Approved",
    "utme_requirements": "<p>The <strong>UTME subjects</strong> shall include English Language, Mathematics, and any 2 from Geography, Economics, Government, Biology, Physics, and Chemistry.</p>",
    "de_requirements": "<p class=\"ql-align-justify\">  In addition to meeting the minimum O’ Level requirements, Direct Entry candidates into 200 Level must meet any of the following conditions: </p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Two (2) A Level passes in Geography and other relevant subject OR Two merit passes in Geography and one other subject at NCE Level.</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Candidates without Geography at A Level, but with credit pass in Geography at O’ Level may be considered but must still have another A Level pass in one Social Science or Science.</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Holders of OND in Urban and Regional Planning, Town Planning, Cartography, Environmental/Science Management, Meteorology, Transport and Logistics Studies/Management, Hospitality and Tourism Management, Geoinformatics, and Agriculture may be considered for direct entry admission into 200 Level.</p><p>  </p>",
    "subjects": "<p class=\"ql-align-justify\">The minimum O’ Level subjects requirements for any of the two programmes shall be 5 credit passes at one or two sittings in SSCE/NECO <strong>in English Language, Mathematics, and any other 3 subjects from Science or Social Science.</strong></p><p><br></p>",
    "remarks": ""
  },
